{%- comment -%}
  CAVIERA ceremonial loader — MENU → THE HOUSE revision.

  IMPORTANT CHANGE from the previous revision: this no longer plays automatically when the
  website first loads, on refresh, or once-per-session — none of that logic exists any more. It
  is now tied to one deliberate action only: clicking THE HOUSE inside the full-screen menu (see
  the data-caviera-house-link attribute in sections/caviera-header.liquid and the click handler in
  assets/caviera-header.js). Since THE HOUSE can be opened from any page, this snippet is now
  rendered globally (every page, via layout/theme.liquid — no longer inside a
  template.name == 'index' gate) rather than homepage-only.

  The video is the same approved asset (assets/caviera-loader-oryx-2026.mp4) as the retired
  homepage-load revision — only the trigger changed, not the artwork or the visual treatment.

  assets/caviera-loader.js exposes window.CaviearaLoader.show(onComplete) — a small, reusable,
  idempotent public API. The root element always renders unconditionally (when settings.
  enable_loader is on); the script decides at runtime whether a call to .show() actually plays the
  video (respecting prefers-reduced-motion — navigates immediately instead of forcing the walk —
  and every failure/safety fallback), so a blocked/failed script, or nobody ever calling .show(),
  never overlays or blocks any page. No decorative graphics, no House Seal, no Master Signature —
  the walking Oryx video is the only visual event, exactly as approved.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.enable_loader -%}
  <div class="caviera-loader" data-caviera-loader aria-hidden="true">
    <video
      class="caviera-loader__video"
      data-loader-video
      src="{{ 'caviera-loader-oryx-2026.mp4' | asset_url }}"
      muted
      playsinline
      preload="metadata"
    ></video>
  </div>
  <script src="{{ 'caviera-loader.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
